A||||6||8Ball||Pontiac and Recall work||||8||
Z||000000||8Ball||08-22-2001||03:12 PM||||Well It is apparent that my Fiero has never has the recall work done on it. So I started the quest to get a dealership to do it. They ALL told me eventually they do not work on Fiero's. So I called 1800-pmcares (Yea sure they do!!)<BR>This did me no good as the lady informed me that no matter what the law is that after 12 years NO ONE will do the recall work for me. <BR>And further more she has no way to look up my vin to verify that I even need the recall work so so I am (in her words) SOL!!!!<P>What a crock.<BR>Any ideas on what steps to take next?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Randy||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cheever3000||08-22-2001||03:20 PM||||At least when I called the same number, the guy was able to look up my VIN (then again, mine are both 88's).  But he said there's no outstanding recall for my vehicle.  I told him the VIN is within the range of numbers for the recall as stated in their own bulletins - but he said it boiled down to the fact that some of those get it and some don't.  All he could tell me was that for MY vehicle there is no recall outstanding, or maybe his word was pending.  The bottom line is, if I want it done I will have to pay for it myself.<P>Oh, and here on the Forum last year sometime, I was told there is NO EXPIRATION on SAFETY recalls.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||08-22-2001||04:05 PM||||What a difference a year makes!  In 1996 (or so), I called 1-800-PMCARES, and gave them the VIN number of my 1987 Fiero GT.  The person who took my call was nothing but friendly, helpful and professional.  When she couldn't get the information for me immediately, she even offered to call me back long distance.  I told her that would be fine.<P>She called me back a little later, and had  answers for all of my questions.  The recall was still active, had not been performed on my vehicle, and Pontiac would do it free of charge.  I just had to make an appointment with one of my local dealerships.  Great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Unfortunately, I didn't want to be without the car, and delayed scheduling an appointment for a year or more.  Finally I decided the time was right to have it done (especially since I found two broken bolts in the forward exhaust manifold!).<P>Called 1-800-PMCARES again to reconfirm - totally different attitude than before!  A  stern-sounding lady informed me that there were <B>no</B> outstanding recalls on my car.  Told her that was interesting, because a year earlier I called the same number, gave them the same VIN number, and was told I could have the recall performed free of charge-!  She just repeated, "There are <B>no</B> outstanding recalls on that VIN."<P>I didn't feel like arguing, and supposed that she probably was told to say that line (wasn't her idea).  Just doing her job.  So I said, "I see," or something, and hung up.<P>In retrospect, I'm kind of glad that I'm doing the recall work myself.  I'll probably do a more careful job than a typical dealership, and it's a learning experience if nothing else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.      ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||08-22-2001||05:45 PM||||Hey guys,<P>This has been gone over lots, and I've been following it all!  I finally got my recall stuff done about five months ago, after four months of hassle with it.  Here are some links that will be more helpful:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006081.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006081.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006503.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006503.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010230.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010230.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010706.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010706.html</A> <P>These pages have more links on them that lead to even more useful information.<P>Just in case you don't see it on the other pages, Pontiac has purged all information on Fieros from their computers.  They no longer have record if your car has had the recall work performed or not.  The computer shows no open recalls, therefore they assume it's been done.  The only way to get the work performed is to get your car visually inspected and approved for the work by a dealership.  The <B>MOST IMPORTANT</B> advice I could give you is this: if you call 1800pmcares and get a good service person, ALWAYS request that they call you back in X days when you will have contacted the dealership, so that they may follow up.  If you request them to call back, you will deal with the same helpful person (you cannot call and request to talk to a certain person or an extension).  If you get a poor customer service person, don't request them to call back, but call back when you're ready in hopes of finding a more helpful person.  THE CUSTOMER SERVICE REP. THAT YOU DEAL WITH WILL MAKE OR BREAK WHETHER YOU ARE HELPED OR NOT.  I had a poor dealership I was dealing with, but the customer service rep. made the difference.<P>Good luck!  If you have more questions or need some more help, just let us know.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||8Ball||08-22-2001||06:27 PM||||Thanks a million.<BR>I was afraid I was going to have to camp out at the dealership  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> May still have to never know. but IMHO weither the work is vital or not the law is the law and the law says they HAVE to do the recall work.<BR>That and I am pissy when I don't get my way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000005||dlancer407||08-22-2001||08:07 PM||||Hi 8Ball; Sorry to hear about your problem. I bought a 1985 GT in June of this year. I found out about the recall on another website. I live in Cincinnati Oh. I took my car to Walker Pontiac to have it checked out. They told me the same thing about there being no outstanding recalls on my car. Mine still had the rubber strip on the deck lid also. I called Pontiac Customer service and talked to a very nice lady. She told me to take it back to the dealer to have it visually inspected to see if it had ever been done. I did that and they decided it had not been done. The service tech went right to the parts department and ordered the kit to fix it.They got it in a couple of days and fixed my car without any hassle.I can tell you that A) THE PARTS ARE STILL AVAILABLE B) THE LADY ON THE PHONE FROM PONTIAC TOLD ME THAT SAFETY RECALLS NEVER EXPIRE. If I were you I would call the NHTSA and complain to them, If there are any consumer advocates or reporters in your area contact them. Hell I might even call my local Congressman and tell him you don't want to burn up in your own car! Good luck. If you go to the MIchigan Fiero web site you can print out the whole recall notice, it is about 13 pages long. I know in that notice it states that this recall will be done regardless of age, mileage, ownership from this time on. ( NO MENTION OF 8 YEARS )||||reg||6
Z||000006||tgowens||08-23-2001||02:06 AM||||8Ball, I have recall information on my web site......  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/my_links.html" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero/my_links.html</A> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocks_sig.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
